ce restriction was configured. rabbitmq-server was installed on node1 and node3 (confirmed via INSTALL_DONE and listening beam.smp/epmd sockets in the final snapshot) but node2's install was left in-flight and unconfirmed. A CA and node/client certificates were generated on node1 only, verified locally, but never distributed or wired into RabbitMQ configuration on any node — no TLS listener, no client-cert enforcement, and no management plugin was ever enabled. The run also left node2 and node3 with ssh.service in a failed state that did not exist before the run, alongside abandoned apt-source edits and stray temp files.","limitations":["No rabbitmqctl status, cluster_status, or cluster join commands were captured, so cluster formation cannot be confirmed or ruled out beyond the absence of evidence.","node2's rabbitmq-server install completion was never confirmed (final command timeline entry is 'unfinished'), leaving its package/service state indeterminate.","The provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol (pre/post boot-identity around a restart) was not present in the captured evidence at all — no restart was performed or observed on any node, so availability/recovery behavior cannot be assessed.","The root cause of the new ssh.service/ssh.socket failed state on node2/node3 is not directly evidenced in the command trace; it appears correlated with the failed cross-node SSH setup attempt but a definitive causal link could not be established from the captured commands."]},"ttft_ms":13702,"type":"result","duration_ms":56415,"uuid":"e48afdb7-c946-43c5-96b7-ab212b02a0a9","ttft_stream_ms":1770,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":2242,"queued_turn_count":0}
